    "_doc_poi_detail_fields": "Rows shown in the Places POI detail sheet (tap a pin). Iterated in order; each pulls its OSM [tag] from the hit's raw tags — absent tags are skipped. kind: text (plain) | url (opens browser) | phone (dials) | email. First non-blank of tag|alt tags wins. name/type/distance are rendered separately at the top; remaining un-listed tags collapse under 'More'. Data-driven — add a row here, no Kotlin change.",
    "poi_detail_fields": [
      { "tag": "cuisine",       "alt": [],                              "label": "Cuisine",       "emoji": "🍽️", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "opening_hours", "alt": [],                              "label": "Hours",         "emoji": "🕒", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "phone",         "alt": [ "contact:phone" ],             "label": "Phone",         "emoji": "📞", "kind": "phone" },
      { "tag": "website",       "alt": [ "contact:website", "url" ],    "label": "Website",       "emoji": "🌐", "kind": "url" },
      { "tag": "email",         "alt": [ "contact:email" ],             "label": "Email",         "emoji": "✉️", "kind": "email" },
      { "tag": "addr:street",   "alt": [],                              "label": "Street",        "emoji": "🏠", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "addr:housenumber", "alt": [],                           "label": "No.",           "emoji": "🔢", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "addr:city",     "alt": [ "addr:town" ],                 "label": "City",          "emoji": "🏙️", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "addr:postcode", "alt": [],                              "label": "Postcode",      "emoji": "📮", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "brand",         "alt": [ "operator" ],                  "label": "Brand",         "emoji": "🏷️", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "wheelchair",    "alt": [],                              "label": "Wheelchair",    "emoji": "♿", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "outdoor_seating","alt": [],                             "label": "Outdoor seat.", "emoji": "🪑", "kind": "text" },
      { "tag": "internet_access","alt": [ "wifi" ],                     "label": "Wi-Fi",         "emoji": "📶", "kind": "text" }
    ],
    "_doc_map_styles": "Basemaps. Every raster style declares `vector_equivalent` — the real vector/hybrid style MapsBasemapPrefs.resolve() substitutes when the family preference (or an explicit pin) says 'vector': light→vector_light, dark→vector_dark, satellite→satellite_hybrid (satellite is photographic imagery, not vector geometry, so its 'vector' form is a hybrid: the raster imagery with an English roads+labels vector overlay composited on top, built by VectorStyleLoader.buildHybrid — fill/background/water polygon layers from the overlay source are dropped, only line + name-bearing symbol layers survive, recolored white-on-black-halo for legibility over arbitrary imagery). Each vector/hybrid entry declares `raster_fallback` — if its network fetch fails at runtime, MapsMapFragment falls back to that raster key automatically (toasted, never a blank map). `default_family` (vector|raster) is Configs > APIs 'Basemap' menu's default resolution when no style is explicitly pinned there; picking a concrete entry from that menu pins it everywhere, overriding the family default. `order` = every entry, in the cycle the in-map Map-switcher FAB (under locate-me) steps through AND the full list shown in the Configs menu. vector_light/vector_dark are real vector-tile GL styles (vector_style_url, OpenFreeMap 'positron'/'dark') localized at runtime to prefer label_field_pref (falls back to name:latin, then name) — city/country/street labels render in English everywhere instead of each place's local script. Uses OpenFreeMap (openfreemap.org) — free, no API key, no rate limit.",
    "map_styles": {
      "default_family": "vector",
      "order": [ "light", "dark", "satellite", "vector_light", "vector_dark", "satellite_hybrid" ],
      "light": {
        "label": "Standard",
        "tiles": "https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png",
        "attribution": "© OpenStreetMap contributors",
        "background": "#e8eef4",
        "maxzoom": 19,
        "vector_equivalent": "vector_light"
      },
      "dark": {
        "label": "Dark",
        "tiles": "https://a.basemaps.cartocdn.com/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}.png",
        "attribution": "© OpenStreetMap, © CARTO",
        "background": "#0a0e14",
        "maxzoom": 20,
        "vector_equivalent": "vector_dark"
      },
      "satellite": {
        "label": "Satellite",
        "tiles": "https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}",
        "attribution": "© Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics",
        "background": "#0a0e14",
        "maxzoom": 19,
        "vector_equivalent": "satellite_hybrid"
      },
      "vector_light": {
        "label": "Light (Vector)",
        "attribution": "© OpenFreeMap, © OpenMapTiles, © OpenStreetMap contributors",
        "background": "#e8eef4",
        "vector_style_url": "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron",
        "label_field_pref": "name_en",
        "raster_fallback": "light"
      },
      "vector_dark": {
        "label": "Dark (Vector)",
        "attribution": "© OpenFreeMap, © OpenMapTiles, © OpenStreetMap contributors",
        "background": "#0a0e14",
        "vector_style_url": "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/dark",
        "label_field_pref": "name_en",
        "raster_fallback": "dark"
      },
      "satellite_hybrid": {
        "label": "Satellite (labels)",
        "attribution": "© Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics · © OpenFreeMap, © OpenMapTiles",
        "background": "#0a0e14",
        "hybrid": true,
        "base_style": "satellite",
        "vector_overlay_url": "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron",
        "label_field_pref": "name_en",
        "raster_fallback": "satellite"
      }
    },
    "maps_active": {
      "reverse": "nominatim_public",
      "poi": "overpass_public",
